  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper evaluates hybrid PPO reinforcement‑learning trading agents using three 4‑qubit variational quantum architectures (QNN, QRWKV, QASA) on Taiwan stock market sector‑rotation data (2007–2025). Although quantum models achieved higher training rewards (e.g., QASA 2883.3 vs LSTM 2737.0), they produced worse financial outcomes, with cumulative returns of 93.14–105.93% and Sharpe ratios 0.71–0.78 compared to LSTM and Transformer returns of ~124–125% and Sharpe ≈0.88. The study concludes that quantum models overfit the proxy reward signal and do not outperform classical baselines.",
